WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.322 line:4% position:50% align:center
I remember when these fields were green...

00:00:03.583 --> 00:00:05.279 line:4% position:50% align:center
Before the droughts started.

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:08.191 line:4% position:50% align:center
As trapped greenhouse gases warmed the planet,

00:00:08.191 --> 00:00:12.553 line:4% position:50% align:center
heatwaves lasted longer and evaporated water right out of the soil.

00:00:12.813 --> 00:00:16.443 line:4% position:50% align:center
NASA’s SMAP satellite watched Earth's soil moisture drop from space,

00:00:16.443 --> 00:00:20.200 line:4% position:50% align:center
showing how farms across the world were drying out into dust.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.961 line:4% position:50% align:center
Then came the smoke.

00:00:22.435 --> 00:00:24.935 line:4% position:50% align:center
Every summer, dried-out forests caught fire

00:00:24.935 --> 00:00:27.876 line:4% position:50% align:center
easier and burned hotter than ever before.

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:32.113 line:4% position:50% align:center
Tiny smoke particles, called aerosols, floated high into the sky,

00:00:32.113 --> 00:00:35.200 line:4% position:50% align:center
blocking the sunlight plants needed to grow.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:41.741 line:4% position:50% align:center
Firestorms grew so huge they created their own weather, blasting smoke past

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:46.327 line:4% position:50% align:center
the rain clouds into the stratosphere, where it stayed trapped for years.

00:00:46.927 --> 00:00:50.579 line:4% position:50% align:center
NASA’s FIRMS fire maps lit up red across every continent...

00:00:51.179 --> 00:00:54.717 line:4% position:50% align:center
We watched the warning signs, until there was nowhere left to run.
